+// hadHandshake reports whether a handshake with the peer has ever completed.
+//
+// Safe Launcher: the persistent keepalive is sent at once only to a peer that has been in use. The launcher's core
+// holds the connections of every application in its settings, running or not, and an immediate keepalive of an
+// unused one would start a handshake that takes the session away from another client with the same key (such as
+// the WireGuard or AmneziaVPN application). Such a peer stays silent until something is sent through it; from then
+// on its keepalives go as usual.
+func (peer *Peer) hadHandshake() bool {
+	return peer.lastHandshakeNano.Load() != 0
+}
